senses.gloss:
(I)--a son of सोमापी;
1: भा. IX. २२. 9.
ruled for ६७ years;
2: Br. III. ७४. १११.
father of अयुतायु.
3: Vi. IV. २३. 4.

(III)--a daughter of शूर and भोजा;
1: M. ४६. 4, 6.
a sister of Vasudeva and queen of दमघोष, the Cedi king;
2: भा. IX. २४. ३० and ३९; Br. III. ७१. १५० and १५८; Vi. IV. १४. ३१, ४४-5.
mother of शिसुपाल; a वीरमाता.
3: वा. ९६. १४९, १५७-8.

(I)--the Vedas: interpreted in two ways in the द्वापर;
1: Br. II. ३१. 6, ७२; ३२, ३५; IV. 6. ६४; M. ५२. १२; १४४. 7; वा. ३४. ९५; ३९. ११; ४१. ९०; ५५. 7; ६१. ७५; ७६. 3; १००. ३३; १०१. 9, २२, ५७.
the same, ऋग्, Yajus, and साम in every manvan- tara though in different redactions; here are four stotras-- Dravyastotram, गुणस्तोत्रम्, Karmastotram, and Abhi- janastotram; above all these is Brahmastotram; mantras were originally five fold;
2: M. १४५. ५८-63.
having learnt the श्रौत from their predecessors the seven sages repeated the same.
3: वा. 3. 8; ३२. ४४; ५९. ३१.
